# config/Kconfig.relibc — the C library for ported C programs
#
# relibc is the porting layer for C code (plan decision D12), built outside the
# kernel: this symbol only decides whether `make relibc` builds it, for the ISA
# of the configuration it is read from (one .config is one ISA; the Makefile reads
# each ISA's own: RV_USER_KCONFIG, AARCH64_USER_KCONFIG, X86_64_KCONFIG).

menu "C library (relibc)"

config RELIBC
    bool "relibc: libc.a and the test C programs (make relibc)"
    default n
    depends on !HWCLASS_EMBEDDED
    help
      `make relibc` builds the pinned relibc (third_party/RELIBC_PIN, checked
      out by tools/relibc_fetch.sh outside the repository; make never
      downloads) with the `azos` platform layer of userspace/lib/relibc-azos,
      and the C programs of userspace/tests/relibc against it with `zig cc`,
      into build/relibc/<isa>/. It refuses, naming what is missing, without
      zig, cbindgen or the checkout, and for an ISA whose configuration leaves
      this off. The build is also the only compile check the platform layer
      has: it is not part of any other crate.

      Off by default, and not on a small board (HWCLASS_EMBEDDED): relibc
      brings a heap allocator, threads and a per-process descriptor table, none
      of which a board of that class has room for. The programs are not on a
      volume image yet: the kernel runs an image only when a seccomp row binds
      its digest, and these have none.

endmenu
